{"id": "EUVD-2026-95907", "enisaUuid": "a72209c2-f919-38f7-bfa1-506d3807a680", "description": "AstronRPA through 1.1.6 contains a cross-site scripting vulnerability in the desktop client's smart-component chat that allows remote attackers to execute OS commands by abusing unsanitized LLM output rendered via v-html. Attackers can embed prompt-injection content in a web page so the model emits HTML event handlers invoking the unrestricted open-path IPC handler with shell metacharacters, executing commands as the desktop user.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T16:04:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:58:15", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa/issues/892", "https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa/blob/8b015bc1b15d23fbdc55c78ff1de9af4bb65fba6/frontend/packages/web-app/src/components/SmartComponent/hooks/useChatContext.tsx#L203", "https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/astronrpa-through-1.1.6-rce-via-smart-component-chat-xss-and-ipc-bridge"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gwjf-3fv9-8jxc", "CVE-2026-108159"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8116be78-8c11-3c25-b4ca-cf4adc54168b", "product": {"name": "astron-rpa", "vendor": {"name": "iflytek"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.1.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bdba3251-7cc2-3821-8409-dc0fa4b296b9", "vendor": {"name": "iflytek"}}], "isExploited": false}